:"Housing Overview and Scrutiny Committee","time":"10.00 am","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://northumberland.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-10-20","committee":"Firefighters' Pension Scheme Local Pension Board","time":"11.30 am","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://northumberland.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-11-04","committee":"County Council","time":"2.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://northumberland.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-11-05","committee":"Family and Children's Services Overview and Scrutiny Committee","time":"10.00 am","status":"Provisional","webcast":false,"url":"https://northumberland.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-11-10","committee":"Cabinet","time":"10.00 am","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://northumberland.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-11-18","committee":"Standing Advisory Council on Religious Education (SACRE)","time":"4.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://northumberland.moderngov.co.uk"}],"recent":[{"date":"2026-09-03","committee":"Family and Children's Services Overview and Scrutiny Committee","time":"10.00 am","status":"Provisional","webcast":false,"url":"https://northumberland.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-08","committee":"Cabinet","time":"10.00 am","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://northumberland.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-08","committee":"Cabinet Shareholder Committee","time":"10.30 am","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://northumberland.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-16","committee":"County Council","time":"3.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://northumberland.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-17","committee":"Housing Overview and Scrutiny Committee","time":"10.00 am","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://northumberland.moderngov.co.uk"}]},"news":[],"news_drafts":[{"headline":"Northumberland borrows more despite cutting capital spending as reserves drain","lead":"Northumberland County Council increased its external borrowing by \u00a364 million in the year to March 2026 while reducing its cash reserves by \u00a317 million and holding back \u00a3134 million of planned capital spending. External debt rose from \u00a3831 million to \u00a3895 million even though the underlying financing requirement \u2014 the amount the council actually needed to borrow for long-term assets \u2014 increased by only \u00a343 million. The council's schools funding deficit more than doubled to \u00a320 million, and it drew down other reserves to cover day-to-day costs. Capital spending ran 11 per cent below budget, with the council deferring projects. The mismatch signals the council is relying on borrowed money to fund running costs rather than investment in long-lived assets.","iso":"2026-09-16","paper_title":"03.1 Appendix 1 Treasury Management Annual Report for the Financial Year 25 26","paper_url":"https://northumberland.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s32970/32970.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true}],"findings":[{"iso":"2026-09-23","committee":"Audit and Standards Committee","paper_title":"Appendix 1 for Annual Report from Audit and Standards Committee to Council","paper_url":"https://northumberland.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s33147/33147.pdf","headline":"Adult Social Care and Children's Services received a high proportion of 'Outstanding' and 'Good' inspection ratings.","detail":"Committee noted that Adult Social Care and Children's Services inspections resulted in a high proportion rated as 'Outstanding' or 'Good', indicating strong service performance in these major cost areas.","category":"governance","matters":"Strong inspection ratings in social care reduce risk of service failure and associated financial pressure, supporting the council's operational and financial sustainability.","figures":"none","quote":"The Committee noted the high proportion of inspections resulting in a rating of 'Outstanding' or 'Good'","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-23","committee":"Audit and Standards Committee","paper_title":"Appendix 1 for Annual Report from Audit and Standards Committee to Council","paper_url":"https://northumberland.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s33147/33147.pdf","headline":"Internal Audit provided a 'Reasonable' opinion on the governance framework and the Committee questioned aspects of audit coverage.","detail":"Chief Internal Auditor gave a 'Reasonable' opinion on adequacy and effectiveness of governance, risk management and control arrangements for 2024/25. Committee queried aspects of Internal Audit's coverage and the assurances underpinning the opinion.","category":"audit","matters":"When an audit committee questions the scope and coverage of internal audit work, this can signal gaps in assurance over the control environment.","figures":"none","quote":"A 'Reasonable' opinion was provided and the Committee queried aspects of Internal Audit's coverage and assurances for the opinion provided.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-23","committee":"Audit and Standards Committee","paper_title":"Appendix 1 for Annual Report from Audit and Standards Committee to Council","paper_url":"https://northumberland.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s33147/33147.pdf","headline":"External auditor issued unqualified opinion on 2024/25 accounts with no significant weaknesses identified.","detail":"Forvis Mazars completed audit of the 2024/25 financial statements and annual report, resulting in an unqualified opinion. No significant weaknesses were identified by the external auditor.","category":"audit","matters":"An unqualified audit opinion with no significant weaknesses is fundamental reassurance to lenders that accounts are fairly stated and financial controls are sound.","figures":"none","quote":"no significant weaknesses were identified by the external auditor","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-16","committee":"County Council","paper_title":"Treasury Management Annual Report for the Financial Year 2025-26 (2)","paper_url":"https://northumberland.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s32969/32969.pdf","headline":"\u00a317 million of LOBO loans carry call dates in 2026-27, creating quantified refinancing exposure.","detail":"The council holds \u00a389 million of LOBO loans (weighted average rate 3.72%), of which \u00a317 million has call dates within the next 12 months. Market forecasts indicate interest rates will decrease in 2026-27. If rates fall and lenders exercise call options, the council will need to refinance at prevailing market rates.","category":"borrowing","matters":"LOBO call risk represents quantified refinancing exposure. Falling rates increase call probability, potentially forcing refinancing and triggering treasury management decisions outside normal planning.","figures":"Total LOBO loans \u00a389m; LOBO loans at call risk in 2026-27: \u00a317m","quote":"The LOBO loans with a risk of being called in 2026-27 total \u00a317.000 million.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-16","committee":"County Council","paper_title":"Treasury Management Annual Report for the Financial Year 2025-26 (2)","paper_url":"https://northumberland.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s32969/32969.pdf","headline":"Advance Northumberland financial restructure did not proceed, deferred from 2025-26 as planned.","detail":"The budget assumed income reduction from a proposed financial restructure of Advance Northumberland (the council's major trading company) but this transaction did not occur. Third-party loan income exceeded budget by \u00a33.134 million as a result, and MRP charges were \u00a32.148 million higher than budgeted because the restructure did not happen.","category":"governance","matters":"Postponement of a planned major transaction involving a significant council entity raises questions about the state of the trading company and why financial restructuring budgeted for 2025-26 was deferred.","figures":"Third-party loan income \u00a319.220m actual (\u00a33.134m above budget of \u00a316.086m); MRP \u00a32.148m higher than budget","quote":"The budget assumed a reduction in investment income following the proposed financial restructure of Advance Northumberland; however, the restructure did not proceed during 2025-26, resulting in higher income than forecast.","material":true}],"editorial":null,"freshness":{"last_paper_iso":"2026-09-16"},"name":"Northumberland UA","daily_post":{"iso":"2026-09-19","since_iso":"2026-08-20","distress":false,"headline":"\u00a317 million of LOBO loans carry call dates in 2026-27, creating quantified refinancing exposure.","lead":"LOBO call risk represents quantified refinancing exposure. Falling rates increase call probability, potentially forcing refinancing and triggering treasury management decisions outside normal planning.","also":["34 other findings in this window"],"watch":"Audit and Standards Committee on 2026-09-23","n_findings":35,"n_documents":0,"top_paper_title":"Treasury Management Annual Report for the Financial Year 2025-26 (2)","top_paper_url":"https://northumberland.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s32969/32969.pdf","draft":true},"findings_total":133,"news_drafts_total":1}}